source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "Accountability is enforced via strict bifurcation of inquiry (model-driven) and governance (state-committed). This design prevents models from subverting the research record by ensuring that only valid, rule-compliant transitions are committed to durable history.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "49bbe331dc9a55dbc43ac9110f2b61ec7a62aab0742609bfec08dcb36e11cc95", "hash": "7468121afbbd255ae4c9b8b943e6a53667b731acdabb0def750b7eaf2207b15d"}, {"seq": 3214, "time": "2026-10-29T06:27:58.667430+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 32023, "provider_input_hash": "8bd630d591706278a53e84c12cdbeaa85e302404b7c56e901da2869d389359a6", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "